  "tajweedCoursesTitle": "Tajweed Rules",
  "tajweedCoursesIntro": "Tajweed (تجويد) is the set of rules that govern correct pronunciation of the Quran. Below are the core rules every reciter should know.",
  "tajweedCoursesInteractive": "Interactive lessons",
  "tajweedRuleMaddTitle": "Madd (المدّ) — Elongation",
  "tajweedRuleMaddDescription": "Prolonging a vowel sound by 2, 4, or 6 counts depending on the type. Madd Tabi'i is the natural elongation of 2 counts.",
  "tajweedRuleGhunnahTitle": "Ghunnah (الغُنّة) — Nasalization",
  "tajweedRuleGhunnahDescription": "A nasal sound produced when pronouncing letters Noon (ن) or Meem (م) with shaddah, held for about 2 counts.",
  "tajweedRuleIdghamTitle": "Idgham (الإدغام) — Merging",
  "tajweedRuleIdghamDescription": "Merging a Noon Sakinah or Tanween into one of the letters: ي، ر، م، ل، و، ن. The merging may include Ghunnah depending on the letter.",
  "tajweedRuleIkhfaTitle": "Ikhfa (الإخفاء) — Concealment",
  "tajweedRuleIkhfaDescription": "Hiding the sound of Noon Sakinah or Tanween between Idgham and Izhar when followed by any of 15 specific letters, with Ghunnah.",
  "tajweedRuleIqlabTitle": "Iqlab (الإقلاب) — Conversion",
  "tajweedRuleIqlabDescription": "Converting a Noon Sakinah or Tanween into a hidden Meem when followed by the letter Ba (ب), with Ghunnah.",
  "tajweedRuleQalqalaTitle": "Qalqala (القلقلة) — Echoing",
  "tajweedRuleQalqalaDescription": "A bouncing echo sound on the letters: ق، ط، ب، ج، د when they have a sukoon. Stronger at the end of a verse.",
